 "reading": {
  "the_mirror_is_a_rebuild": "the family-B table STRUCTURE mirrors exactly (10 tables, same offsets+counts+entry sizes) but the blob BODIES are window-specific: 72/76 paired keys changed at identical sizes, 4 identical — the lower window's second table set is not a copy of the upper's, it is a parallel build of the same release (ring 17's 'two different builds', now proven at the PSP layer)",
  "table_mirrors_relocated": "0/10 tables byte-identical — expected: the lower copies relocate the entry addresses into their own window; the fidelity question lives at the blob level, and there the answer is: rebuilt, not copied",
  "deeper_than_ffs": "ring 17's FFS pairing measured 261/380 shared GUIDs byte-identical across the windows; the PSP layer measures 3.69% byte-stability — the PSP layer is the most window-specific layer of the image, extending ring 13's cross-release churn lesson WITHIN one release",
  "combo_completed": "both windows carry both chip families' routing: the lower window holds the family-A primaries (8 tables) plus family-B's tables (10), the upper holds family-B (10); the 33 lower-only blob types are family-A binaries with no upper-window counterpart (and 0 upper-only)",
  "stable_core": "the 4 identical paired blobs include the 4,096-B type-0x22 policy table — the window-invariant plumbing the PSP keeps byte-stable even across builds"
 },
 "honesty": [
  "the family attribution (lower=Zen/Zen+, upper=Zen2/Zen3) is ring 17's, inherited — this probe adds the blob-type pairing, not the family naming",
  "pairing is per (magic, type, subprogram) first occurrence per window; sizes are recorded for audit",
  "entries resolving outside the 32-MiB ROM are skipped (counted missing, never read)",
  "'changed' means blob BYTES differ at equal (or recorded) size — the rebuild reading is structural, no per-blob semantic diff was run",
  "psptool's fletcher validation gates every table; the upper parse required slicing the window (psptool's 32-MiB FET walk misses it — the two FET warnings are the visible trace)"
 ]
}
